menu "Godwit dial"

choice GODWIT_DIAL_SIDE
    prompt "Which dial this firmware is for"
    default GODWIT_DIAL_SIDE_LEFT
    help
      Set by the dial-left and dial-right projects in their
      sdkconfig.defaults. The head unit reads it from the dial's
      DIAL_FEATURE_INFO report to tell the two apart, and it is in the USB
      product name ("Godwit Dial Left" / "Godwit Dial Right").

config GODWIT_DIAL_SIDE_LEFT
    bool "Left"

config GODWIT_DIAL_SIDE_RIGHT
    bool "Right"

endchoice

config GODWIT_DIAL_HOST_TIMEOUT_MS
    int "Standby after this long without a ring frame (ms)"
    range 200 10000
    default 1500
    help
      The head unit sends ~30 ring frames a second. When none arrives for
      this long the dial shows its own standby face until they resume.

endmenu
